-- title:
--   Completed stalk of the two-chart model at a dominated point
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $F$ a field with an $R$-algebra structure, and $j \in F$ with $j \neq 0$. Write $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,R\,F\,j$ for the $R$-subalgebra of $F$ consisting of the elements of $F$ that are integral over the $R$-subalgebra generated by $j$, and $X_{\mathrm{fin}} = \operatorname{Spec}$ of that algebra. Let $y$ be a point of $X_{\mathrm{fin}}$, i.e. a prime ideal $\mathfrak{p}_y$ of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,R\,F\,j$, and assume that the image of $y$ under the underlying map of the morphism `ιFin R F j` into the two-chart integral model $\mathrm{TwoChartIntegralModel}\,R\,F\,j$ (the pushout of `fFin R F j` and `fInf R F j`) lies in the open image of $\top$ under `ιFin R F j`. Let $B$ be a commutative ring and $\kappa : B \to \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,R\,F\,j$ an injective ring homomorphism which dominates at $y$ in the sense that for every $c$ in the chart algebra there are $b, d \in B$ with $\kappa d \notin \mathfrak{p}_y$ and $c \cdot \kappa d = \kappa b$; assume moreover that $\mathfrak{m} = \kappa^{-1}(\mathfrak{p}_y)$ is a maximal ideal of $B$. Let $\mathrm{STK}$ be the stalk of the structure sheaf of the two-chart integral model at the image point, and let $\mathrm{germY}$ be the ring homomorphism from the chart algebra to $\mathrm{STK}$ obtained by composing the inverse of `Scheme.ΓSpecIso`, the inverse of the $\top$-component isomorphism `(ιFin R F j).appIso ⊤`, and the germ map at the open image of $\top$. Then there is a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of $\mathrm{STK}$ along its maximal ideal (as a local ring) onto the adic completion of $B$ along $\mathfrak{m}$, such that for every $b \in B$ the image under $e$ of the canonical image of $\mathrm{germY}(\kappa b)$ in the completed stalk is the canonical image of $b$ in $\mathrm{AdicCompletion}\,\mathfrak{m}\,B$.
--
--   This identifies the completed local ring of the two-chart integral model at a point of the $j$-finite chart with the $\mathfrak{m}$-adic completion of any ring $B$ that dominates the chart algebra at that point, compatibly with the two structure maps. It is used in the construction of auxiliary full-level modular curve charts, namely by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_drinfeldChart_baseChange_of_cyclotomicWitness_of_isAlgClosed_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevelOne.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_drinfeldChart_baseChange_of_cyclotomicWitness_of_isAlgClosed_of_isPrimitiveRoot_mul_of_dvd) and [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_drinfeldChart_baseChange_of_cyclotomicWitness_of_isAlgClosed`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_ringEquiv_adicCompletion_stalk_drinfeldChart_baseChange_of_cyclotomicWitness_of_isAlgClosed), where the completed stalk must be recognised as the completion of an explicit package ring.
